DysruptionHub reports: Everett, Massachusetts, closed City Hall to the public Tuesday after a cybersecurity incident affected its internal network and technology systems, shifting most essential employees to another municipal building. The city said in a Monday announcement that it discovered the incident Sunday evening and began working with its technology team and cybersecurity professionals. It did not...
